                  <provenance type="#e"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_387">Newark, Surrey.
                        Augustinian priory of St Mary the Virgin and St Thomas the Martyr.
                        </orgName><p>(fol. 230r) "Hic liber est ecclesie sancte Marie et sancti
                        Thome martyris [?] de ... quem qui furto ...".</p><p>The form of the inscr.
                        shows that the MS. is from the Aug. priory of Newark, Surrey (de novo loco);
                        cf. Bodleain Library, Auct. D.inf.2.10 and Balliol 85 both of which have the
                        ex-libris inscr. "Hic liber est ecclesie sancte marie et beati Thome
                        martyris de nouo loco quem qui furto abstulerit vel sine conscientia eiusdem
                        ecclesie conventus quocumque modo alienauerit sit anathema maranatha
                        Amen."</p></provenance>
